meta {
  name: List teachers
  type: http
  seq: 23
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/teachers
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.school: eq {{schoolCode}}
  res.body.teachers: isArray
  res.body.count: gte 1
}

docs {
  A different list from /staff, not a filtered view of it: these rows carry
  staff_id, not person_id, because a teacher is a specialisation of a staff
  member. To show a teacher's name you need the teacher, its staff row and the
  person behind that.

  core.teachers.read is its own capability for the same reason. A timetabling
  client needs to know who teaches and nothing about employment.
}
